From 0f9c034d142dd7c494bf816acdfc72cefa6054ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Antigravity Repair <antigravity@localhost>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 13:32:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Retry Muse without foreign reasoning state

Meta binds Responses reasoning encrypted_content to the caller that issued it. A Muse account switch therefore makes an otherwise valid history fail with 400 "was not issued to this caller".

Keep the first attempt intact so same-account sessions retain full reasoning continuity. Only after that exact rejection, retry once with the encrypted payloads removed, preserving reasoning summaries and the visible/tool history. Remember the rejected payload hashes for the current caller so later turns pre-strip only those hashes and keep new reasoning issued by the current caller.

This complements fill-first account routing: forced fallback or credential re-login no longer has to kill the conversation, while unrelated 400 errors are returned unchanged.
